course: dictionary
lesson: 15544
title: Superficial: only on the surface
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Superficial means only on the surface, not deep or serious. «The cut was superficial, so a plaster was enough.» The cut is only in the top layer of skin, so it is not serious. Always ask: is this deep, or only on the top?
explain: It can also mean only looking at the outside or the obvious parts. «Sam gave a superficial answer that just copied the words from the page.» Sam did not think deeply about why. A deeper answer would explain why.
explain: Superficial can describe a person too. «Mia was superficial and only cared about her clothes and her hair.» She cared about looks and unimportant things, not deep feelings or ideas. Careful: a superficial likeness looks the same at first, but is different underneath. A dolphin and a shark look alike, but one is a mammal and one is a fish.
fact: Superficial means only on the surface, or only looking at the outside.
fact: «Superficial» is an adjective: superficial, more superficial, most superficial.
fact: A superficial wound is not deep or serious, like «a superficial graze».
fact: A superficial person cares mostly about looks and unimportant things.
fact: A superficial likeness seems the same at first, but is different underneath.
exercise: «The nurse said the graze was superficial, so only a plaster was needed.» What does superficial mean here? | Very deep and serious | Covered in dirt | *Only on the surface, not deep | Painful for a long time
exercise: «Her answer was superficial: it just copied the words from the page.» What does superficial suggest? | It is written in pencil | *It does not think deeply | It is very long | It explains why
exercise: Two animals have a superficial likeness. What does this mean? | They are both mammals | They never meet | They are exactly the same inside and out | *They look alike at first but are different underneath
test: «The hero was superficial, judging everyone only by their clothes.» What does superficial mean? | Very brave | Quiet and shy | Deep and thoughtful | *Caring mostly about looks
test: Ella says a superficial reading is the same as a careful reading. Is she right? | Yes, because reading is always fast | Yes, they are exactly the same | *No, a superficial reading only looks at the obvious parts | No, because a careful reading is always shorter
exam: Which sentence uses superficial correctly? | «The lake was superficial, so deep that no one could swim.» | *«The scratch was superficial and healed in a day.» | «The mountain was superficial, tall and very steep.» | «The song was superficial, long and full of deep feelings.»
